{"questions":[{"question_id":"1l1p7iwfj","paperTitle":"JEE Advanced 2013 Paper 1 Offline","year":2013,"examDate":2013,"subject":"physics","chapter":"heat-and-thermodynamics","chapterGroup":"mechanics","topic":"specific-heat-capacity-calorimetry-and-change-of-state","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"ptwo-rectangular-blocks-having-identical-dimensions-can-jee-advanced-physics-units-and-measurements-bcxxvnhxasgzghk6","content":"<p>Two rectangular blocks, having identical dimensions, can be arranged in either configuration-I or configuration-II as shown in the figure. One of the blocks has thermal conductivity <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.303ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 576 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D705\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D705\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> and the other 2<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.303ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 576 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D705\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D705\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>. The temperature difference between the ends along the x-axis is the same in both the configurations. It takes 9 s to transport a certain amount of heat from the hot end to the cold end in configuration-I. The time to transport the same amount of heat in configuration-II is</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l1rn03t1/dbcebfcb-4750-4547-831e-4f9923909d41/f3c82750-b7e4-11ec-aca9-51ae2c04643b/file-1l1rn03t2.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l1rn03t1/dbcebfcb-4750-4547-831e-4f9923909d41/f3c82750-b7e4-11ec-aca9-51ae2c04643b/file-1l1rn03t2.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2013 Paper 1 Offline Physics - Heat and Thermodynamics Question 37 English\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l1rn03t1/dbcebfcb-4750-4547-831e-4f9923909d41/f3c82750-b7e4-11ec-aca9-51ae2c04643b/file-1l1rn03t2.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l1rn03t1/dbcebfcb-4750-4547-831e-4f9923909d41/f3c82750-b7e4-11ec-aca9-51ae2c04643b/file-1l1rn03t2.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l1rn03t1/dbcebfcb-4750-4547-831e-4f9923909d41/f3c82750-b7e4-11ec-aca9-51ae2c04643b/file-1l1rn03t2.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l1rn03t1/dbcebfcb-4750-4547-831e-4f9923909d41/f3c82750-b7e4-11ec-aca9-51ae2c04643b/file-1l1rn03t2.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l1rn03t1/dbcebfcb-4750-4547-831e-4f9923909d41/f3c82750-b7e4-11ec-aca9-51ae2c04643b/file-1l1rn03t2.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l1rn03t1/dbcebfcb-4750-4547-831e-4f9923909d41/f3c82750-b7e4-11ec-aca9-51ae2c04643b/file-1l1rn03t2.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"2.0 s"},{"identifier":"B","content":"3.0 s"},{"identifier":"C","content":"4.5 s"},{"identifier":"D","content":"6.0 s"}],"correct_options":["A"],"explanation":"<p>Let L and A be length and area of cross-section of each block.</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.18